{#
  The "only one plugin from this group" warning, written once.

  Every page for a plugin in a mutually exclusive group renders this, so the
  wording must not be duplicated per template — it already drifted once, leaving
  the Global Database Failover page saying "any other failover plugin" without
  ever naming the plugin it conflicts with.

  The sentence adapts to how many other plugins the group holds FOR THE CURRENT
  WRAPPER, which is why `others` is passed in already filtered:

    one other  -> names it, because "the other `failover` plugin" is actionable
                  where "any other failover plugin" leaves the reader guessing.
    several    -> lists them in parentheses.
    none       -> falls back to the generic phrasing rather than emitting a
                  sentence with a dangling reference.

  `conflict_error`, when given, names the error the wrapper raises if the
  group's plugins are combined.

  `lead` is the one canonical statement of the rule.
#}
{% macro lead(group_label) -%}
Only one {{ group_label }} plugin may be enabled per connection.
{%- endmacro %}
{% macro exclusivity(group_label, this_code, others, conflict_error=none) -%}
{{ lead(group_label) }} Do not use `{{ this_code }}` together with
{%- if others | length == 1 %} the other `{{ others[0] }}` plugin
{%- elif others | length > 1 %} any of the other {{ group_label }} plugins ({% for c in others %}`{{ c }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
{%- else %} any other {{ group_label }} plugin
{%- endif %} at the same time for the same connection.
{%- if conflict_error %} Configuring more than one raises a `{{ conflict_error }}` at connection initialization.{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% macro exclusivity_footnote(group_label, codes) -%}
{{ lead(group_label) }} The {% for c in codes %}`{{ c }}`{% if not loop.last %}{% if loop.revindex0 == 1 %}{% if codes | length > 2 %},{% endif %} and {% else %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %} plugins each set the connection credential, so enabling more than one conflicts.
{%- endmacro %}
